<%# The hub's chat with Alex on /contact: the engine's agent chat (studio-engine
    docs/AGENT_CHAT.md) on the person's own thread, chat:alex:<user id>, public, with the
    tier from AgentChat::Viewer, answered in-process by HubAgentChatsController. He asks
    what brought the visitor here and directs it (AgentContextBuilder::CONTACT_PAGE_RULE).
    The thread is held shorter here than the engine's 60vh, and hands its overscroll to
    the page, so a long thread cannot hold a phone away from the form below it. %>
<div class="card min-w-0 pb-4 [&_[data-agent-chat-log]]:max-h-[40vh] [&_[data-agent-chat-log]]:overscroll-auto lg:col-start-1 lg:row-start-1"
     data-voice-chat-page data-test="alex-chat-page">
  <%= render "studio/agent_chat/chat", soul: "alex", name: "Alex",
             portrait: safe_image_tag("/agents/alex.webp", alt: "", class: "w-16 h-16 rounded-full object-cover"),
             role: "AI agent · McRitchie Studio",
             empty: admin? ? "What brought you here today? Type it, or hold to talk." : "What brought you here today?" %>
  <%# Hold to talk stays with admins: POST /voice/takes is behind the admin wall. %>
  <% if Studio.voice_transcription && admin? %>
    <%= render "chat/voice", soul: "alex", name: "Alex" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
